  notes: "Manuscript, not yet published. An earlier version, titled
    'Initialisation Sets the Conditioning of LoRA Merging', was submitted to
    the Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research and is kept in JAIR/."

# Listed so that anyone who finds the earlier preprint first knows how it
# relates to this work, and does not attribute to it two claims that do not
# hold up.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "A Rate-Distortion Function for Model Merging"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Pathak"
        given-names: "Sankalp"
      - family-names: "Garg"
        given-names: "Sanjay"
    year: 2026
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21238820"
    notes: "Our earlier preprint. It proposed the closed-form encoder that the
      manuscript above tests as one of its merges. Two of its claims do not
      hold up in the manuscript's pre-registered experiments: that the encoder
      has the lowest worst-task loss of the methods it compared (an advantage
      that came from the shared initialisation of its cohorts), and that
      worst-task NLL tracks the downstream ranking of methods. The manuscript
      does not use its rate-distortion bound."
